WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.360 --> 00:00:05.440
Let’s say you really need
to find reliable information

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:08.640
about the best diet for
high blood pressure,

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:10.800
or heart disease,
or diabetes.

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:12.160
Where do you go?

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:16.720
Do you go to a website
sponsored by Big Pharma

00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:19.520
that wants to sell you
pills to fix your problem?

00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:22.560
Or, do you want
to treat the cause?

00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:26.080
Welcome to the
Nutrition Facts Podcast

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:27.600
with the latest peer-
reviewed research

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:30.400
on the best ways to eat
healthy and live longer.

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:35.680
Did you know that as many as
37% of breast cancer cases

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:40.400
may be attributable to exposure
to bovine leukemia virus?

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:43.280
Here’s our first story.

00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:47.760
The incidence of breast cancer is
continuously increasing worldwide.

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:50.400
In the U.S., this amounted
to a 40 percent increase

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:52.320
in the incidence by the
turn of this century.

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:56.160
Currently, the main approach is
early detection and treatment.

00:00:56.160 --> 00:00:59.760
That’s important, but why not pay
more attention to primary prevention;

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:02.000
in other words, protecting
people from being exposed to

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:04.880
risk factors for breast cancer
so that they never develop

00:01:04.880 --> 00:01:07.040
breast cancer in the ﬁrst place.

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:10.400
“Overall, it is estimated that
20 percent of all human cancers

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:12.240
have an infectious origin.”

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:16.000
Viruses can trigger cancer
by turning on cancer genes

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:18.640
or turning off cancer
suppressing genes,

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:20.960
but they can also
contribute to tumor formation

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:22.880
just by causing chronic inflammation.

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:27.280
Currently, cancer-causing viruses
are considered the major

00:01:27.280 --> 00:01:31.360
plausible hypothesis for a direct
cause of human breast cancer.

00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:33.200
How did we get here?

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:38.720
It all started about 40 years ago
when a professor of virology

00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:43.440
at UC Berkeley learned how mouse
mammary tumor virus was discovered.

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:47.680
Scientists swapped baby mouse pups
from mice with a high incidence

00:01:47.680 --> 00:01:52.080
of mammary cancer with pups from
mouse strains with a low incidence

00:01:52.080 --> 00:01:56.000
and found that the cancer
incidence matched the foster mothers,

00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:57.600
showing it wasn’t genetic.

00:01:57.600 --> 00:01:59.760
“It occurred to me,”
the professor thought,

00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:03.120
“that humans are foster-
nursed on the cow.”

00:02:04.320 --> 00:02:06.880
Bovine leukemia virus (BLV)
had just been identified as a

00:02:06.880 --> 00:02:08.880
cancer-causing cow virus.

00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:12.400
At the time only about 1 in 10
U.S. dairy cows were infected,

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:14.160
but now it’s closer to half.

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:17.120
We started out with
2/3s of herds affected.

00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:19.920
Then, it was more like 80 percent,
based on their milk

00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:24.160
testing positive for the virus, and 100
percent of the larger industrial farms.

00:02:24.160 --> 00:02:28.160
And now, more than 9 out of 10
U.S. herds are affected,

00:02:28.160 --> 00:02:31.840
a continuation of the
historical trend of the persistent

00:02:31.840 --> 00:02:36.320
proliferation of BLV
within U.S. dairy herds.

00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:39.520
We’ve long known that countries
with the highest milk consumption

00:02:39.520 --> 00:02:41.760
also had the highest
breast cancer incidence.

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:45.040
And it’s not just a matchup
between dairy consumption

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:47.840
and breast cancer incidence
on the country level.

00:02:47.840 --> 00:02:52.160
Individual women who are lactose
intolerant and consume less dairy

00:02:52.160 --> 00:02:54.960
also seem to have decreased
risk of breast cancer.

00:02:56.160 --> 00:02:59.280
Oh, but come on, there’s lots
of stuff in milk that could be

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:02.400
contributing to the cancer
risk like saturated fat and the

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:05.280
presence of cancer-promoting
growth hormones like IGF-1.

00:03:06.320 --> 00:03:08.560
Yes, we know bovine leukemia virus

00:03:08.560 --> 00:03:11.440
is present in marketed
beef and dairy products.

00:03:11.440 --> 00:03:14.880
About half of milk and meat samples
turn up positive for the virus.

00:03:15.440 --> 00:03:18.880
In fact, you can sample the virus
straight out of the air on dairy farms,

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:21.200
on surfaces, and in the milk itself.

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:23.840
Most milk is pasteurized,
but many dairy products

00:03:23.840 --> 00:03:26.720
like raw aged cheeses are not.

00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:29.600
And who hasn’t eaten a pink-
in-the-middle hamburger

00:03:29.600 --> 00:03:30.640
at some point in their life?

00:03:31.760 --> 00:03:34.560
Yes, we have evidence that
people are exposed to the virus.

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:38.160
Yes, we have evidence that people
are actively infected with the virus.

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:42.560
But it wasn’t until 2015 that we
learned infection rates were highest

00:03:42.560 --> 00:03:48.640
in cancerous breast tissue, so much
so that as many as 37 percent

00:03:48.640 --> 00:03:51.840
of breast cancer cases may
be attributable to exposure

00:03:51.840 --> 00:03:53.360
to the bovine leukemia virus.

00:03:54.160 --> 00:03:57.040
That was enough for me to
trigger a whole series of videos

00:03:57.040 --> 00:03:59.280
on the role the virus
plays in breast cancer

00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:02.560
and how the meat and dairy
industries responded to the news.

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:06.880
Okay, now that we’re all back up
to speed, what’s the latest update?

00:04:07.440 --> 00:04:09.520
That’s what I’ll cover next.

00:04:12.077 --> 00:04:16.360
In 2015, researchers in California
found bovine leukemia virus (BLV)

00:04:16.360 --> 00:04:19.440
stitched into the DNA of
human breast cancer tumors from

00:04:19.440 --> 00:04:22.640
mastectomies at such higher
rates than was found

00:04:22.640 --> 00:04:25.600
in normal breast tissue taken
from breast reduction surgery

00:04:25.600 --> 00:04:28.640
that they calculated that
as many as 37 percent

00:04:28.640 --> 00:04:31.440
of breast cancer cases
may be attributable to

00:04:31.440 --> 00:04:34.000
bovine leukemia virus exposure,

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:36.000
likely through the
consumption of milk or meat

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:38.400
obtained from infected animals.

00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:40.800
In response, the milk and
meat industries seemed more

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:44.480
concerned about consumer
confidence than consumer cancer.

00:04:45.040 --> 00:04:48.240
But scientifically, the
research priority turned to:

00:04:48.240 --> 00:04:51.200
could the California results be replicated?

00:04:51.840 --> 00:04:55.120
The answer, it turns out, was yes.

00:04:55.120 --> 00:04:59.360
They were replicated among women
in Iran. Replicated in Brazil.

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:03.120
In Australia, the link
was even stronger.

00:05:03.120 --> 00:05:05.120
In Texas, the same thing.

00:05:06.240 --> 00:05:08.080
Women diagnosed with breast cancer

00:05:08.080 --> 00:05:10.640
were found to be so much
more likely to have

00:05:10.640 --> 00:05:13.200
bovine leukemia virus DNA
in their breast tissue

00:05:13.200 --> 00:05:16.640
compared with women without cancer,
that the attributable risk

00:05:16.640 --> 00:05:20.720
was calculated at 51.82 percent,
indicating that this meat

00:05:20.720 --> 00:05:24.080
and dairy virus could be
responsible for at least one-half

00:05:24.080 --> 00:05:27.280
of the breast cancer cases among
the women in Texas they studied.

00:05:28.320 --> 00:05:31.840
All in all, six of the eight
studies performed to date

00:05:31.840 --> 00:05:33.920
found the virus in human breast tissues,

00:05:33.920 --> 00:05:37.360
which suggests strongly that
BLV does infect humans,

00:05:37.360 --> 00:05:39.920
and breasts can be targets of infection.

00:05:40.960 --> 00:05:44.400
Four of the five studies that were
able to compare infection rates

00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:48.720
in cancerous tissue versus normal
breast tissue found the odds

00:05:48.720 --> 00:05:52.960
of finding the virus in the tumors
was on average four times higher.

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:56.560
How does that compare to other
breast cancer risk factors?

00:05:56.560 --> 00:05:58.960
If you go on hormone
replacement for five years,

00:05:58.960 --> 00:06:01.840
you can bump up your breast
cancer risk 30 percent.

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:03.840
If you take the pill for
more than a dozen years,

00:06:03.840 --> 00:06:05.920
your risk may go up 40 percent.

00:06:05.920 --> 00:06:09.600
If you’re obese when you’re older,
your risk can go up 60 percent.

00:06:09.600 --> 00:06:11.600
Having a first degree
relative with breast cancer

00:06:11.600 --> 00:06:12.480
may double your risk,

00:06:13.040 --> 00:06:15.840
But having your breast infected
with bovine leukemia virus

00:06:15.840 --> 00:06:19.840
may quadruple your risk; increase
your risk hundreds of percent.

00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:23.600
The only risk factors more
potent than BLV infection

00:06:23.600 --> 00:06:27.680
were having the BRCA gene
mutations like Angelina Jolie has

00:06:27.680 --> 00:06:30.800
or a high dose of ionizing radiation,

00:06:30.800 --> 00:06:34.880
like being in the wrong place
at decidedly the wrong time.

00:06:36.240 --> 00:06:39.520
Beyond confirmation, one study
suggested that older patients

00:06:39.520 --> 00:06:41.440
had a greater likelihood of testing positive

00:06:41.440 --> 00:06:43.360
for bovine leukemia virus.

00:06:43.360 --> 00:06:46.960
That makes sense if BLV is
from exposure to dairy and meat.

00:06:46.960 --> 00:06:49.200
The older we get, the
more meals we’ve had,

00:06:49.200 --> 00:06:52.480
the more opportunities to
become infected over time.

00:06:52.480 --> 00:06:55.680
Researchers also discovered
that the virus comes first,

00:06:56.400 --> 00:06:59.680
present in some breast
tissues 3 to 10 years

00:06:59.680 --> 00:07:01.600
before cancer was diagnosed.

00:07:01.600 --> 00:07:04.560
“This argues against
the idea of viral invasion

00:07:04.560 --> 00:07:07.760
of already malignant
cells,” quashing the theory

00:07:07.760 --> 00:07:09.680
that maybe the virus is
somehow just attracted

00:07:09.680 --> 00:07:11.200
to the cancer after the fact.

00:07:11.920 --> 00:07:14.240
Could this explain the
consistent findings that

00:07:14.240 --> 00:07:16.960
breast cancer tissue is more
likely to harbor infection?

00:07:16.960 --> 00:07:21.360
Again, the data showed no;
the virus appeared to come first.

00:07:22.400 --> 00:07:25.840
This review doesn’t provide
absolute proof that BLV

00:07:25.840 --> 00:07:28.400
is a cause of breast cancer,
but based on the best

00:07:28.400 --> 00:07:31.520
available balance of evidence,
BLV infection does indeed

00:07:31.520 --> 00:07:33.440
appear to be a breast cancer risk factor.

00:07:34.080 --> 00:07:36.320
The latest revelation is that it’s now

00:07:36.320 --> 00:07:38.320
been found in human blood, too.

00:07:39.120 --> 00:07:41.520
This has a number of potential ramifications.

00:07:41.520 --> 00:07:44.240
Blood banks, for example,
don’t screen for it;

00:07:44.240 --> 00:07:46.880
so, it’s possible you can get it
from consuming meat or dairy

00:07:46.880 --> 00:07:50.400
or getting blood from someone
who consumed meat or dairy.

00:07:51.040 --> 00:07:55.200
This could also mean that BLV could
cause leukemia in people, too.

00:07:55.200 --> 00:07:57.680
It does in chimpanzees.

00:07:57.680 --> 00:08:01.360
Two infant chimps were fed milk
from cows naturally infected

00:08:01.360 --> 00:08:04.640
with the BLV, and they
both died of leukemia.

00:08:05.280 --> 00:08:08.160
We didn’t even know
chimps could get leukemia.

00:08:08.160 --> 00:08:10.560
This certainly suggests the
possibility of transmission or

00:08:10.560 --> 00:08:13.040
induction of leukemia through
the ingestion of milk from

00:08:13.040 --> 00:08:17.120
BLV-infected cows; or blood-
borne spread could carry

00:08:17.120 --> 00:08:18.720
the virus to other organs.

00:08:18.720 --> 00:08:21.600
In cattle, the virus
causes blood cancers,

00:08:21.600 --> 00:08:24.400
but this may just be because
dairy cattle are turned into

00:08:24.400 --> 00:08:26.800
hamburger when they are
still so young, so maybe

00:08:26.800 --> 00:08:29.440
they don’t have time for
tumors to grow in other organs.

00:08:30.400 --> 00:08:34.160
How concerned should we be
about bovine leukemia virus?

00:08:34.800 --> 00:08:38.480
It is not clear yet whether
this is a good news story

00:08:38.480 --> 00:08:40.000
or a bad news story.

00:08:40.000 --> 00:08:43.360
If subsequent studies show that
BLV does cause breast cancer

00:08:43.360 --> 00:08:46.400
in humans, this will have
significant repercussions

00:08:46.400 --> 00:08:48.320
for the dairy and cattle industries.

00:08:48.320 --> 00:08:50.640
But that means there is
something we can do about it.

00:08:51.200 --> 00:08:54.160
Perhaps attempts should be made
to eradicate the infection

00:08:54.160 --> 00:08:57.040
from cattle now, rather than
wait for the final word.

00:08:57.600 --> 00:09:01.760
Twenty-one nations have eradicated
BLV from their dairy cattle.

00:09:01.760 --> 00:09:06.800
In contrast, in the U.S. the BLV
prevalence just keeps going up.

00:09:07.440 --> 00:09:10.240
If the industries are not going
to step up and try to eliminate

00:09:10.240 --> 00:09:12.560
the disease, then the least
they could do is eliminate

00:09:12.560 --> 00:09:15.920
some of the practices that spread
the disease between animals.

00:09:16.480 --> 00:09:19.920
BLV is spread via blood through
contaminated needles,

00:09:20.480 --> 00:09:25.280
saw or gouge dehorners, tattoo pliers,
ear taggers, hoof knives,

00:09:25.280 --> 00:09:28.480
nose tongs, and other tools
of the agribusiness trade.

00:09:29.120 --> 00:09:32.800
Though in view of the
emerging information about BLV

00:09:32.800 --> 00:09:35.120
in human breast cancer, it
may be prudent to encourage

00:09:35.120 --> 00:09:38.000
the complete elimination of BLV in cattle,

00:09:38.000 --> 00:09:39.680
particularly in the dairy industry.

00:09:39.680 --> 00:09:42.800
The hope is that either
way it may help reduce

00:09:42.800 --> 00:09:45.520
the scourge of breast cancer.

